      "observed": "The e-stop buffers are identified by their value/library part as SN74LVC1G07, but their sourcing MPN is U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R, a tri-state push-pull buffer rather than the open-drain 1G07 specified. These outputs are used in the e-stop sink chain.",
      "expected": "The sourced part should be an SN74LVC1G07-compatible open-drain buffer, as specified, so the e-stop sink chain retains the intended open-drain behavior.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "U15 | SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1 | ... MPN=U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "U22 | SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1 | ... MPN=U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "U35 | SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1 | ... MPN=U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "U36 | SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1 | ... MPN=U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "single non-inverting buffers (SN74LVC1G07, parts U15, U22, U35, U36) wired as /OE-controlled sinks"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the listed MPN is used for sourcing, the e-stop chain will have push-pull outputs instead of open-drain sinks. That can cause contention or incorrect signaling when sink outputs are chained or connected to external e-stop circuitry.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The files show a likely reversed MOSFET in the LTC4412 USB power path and a mismatched value for C46 relative to the other Ethernet center-tap capacitors. The e-stop buffer sourcing MPNs also specify a different output type from the open-drain parts described in the specification."
}

